# K4 - Repo topology and shared code. Kata sandbox sketch (plan section 3.6).
# [K4-nn] sketch IDs are recognised by validate_architecture / trace and ignored by the
# CI adl-coverage gate. Never [TR-*]; promotion is decided only at K12 (architecture/REVIEW.md).
DESCRIPTION K4 - what the release branch strips, and which duplicated declarations must agree
CATEGORY Static Coupling
NAMESPACE TrK4NS
DEFINE SYSTEM Total Recall K4 Sandbox AS trk4
    DEFINE COMPONENT Release Tree AS releasetree
    DEFINE COMPONENT Version Declarations AS versions

# Course pp. 26-27, Tasks 1-2: an explicit restriction names each forbidden pair and so only covers
# what someone named; an implicit one denies by default and adds an inventory rule. release.yml
# strips contributor-only paths from the release branch with a named list: the explicit form. A new
# contributor-only file ships to users until someone remembers to add it. Pattern-based and
# inventoried instead:
ASSERT(Release Tree: every tracked path that looks contributor-only (workflows, vitest and stryker configs, __tests__, katas) is on the release.yml strip list) # [K4-01]

# Course p. 27, Task 4: share what changes rarely and must be identical, duplicate what changes
# often. The version string is duplicated on purpose in four places (plugin package.json, Claude
# manifest, Gemini manifest, the npx bootstrap) and made safe by one source and a sync script.
# A duplicate is only safe if every copy is named in the sync and all of them agree.
ASSERT(Version Declarations: the plugin package.json, the Claude manifest, the Gemini manifest and the npx bootstrap declare one version, and sync-version.mjs names every copy) # [K4-02]

# Not re-asserted, answered with existing evidence (answers.md): hooks.json vs hooks.gemini.json
# (hooks-parity.test.ts), the plugin-vs-root install.sh split (the root file is a 6-line shim into
# bin/cli.mjs), the Claude and Gemini manifests (TR-Q3), the esbuild externals (TR-R7).
